# Sevinne's Reclamation: "If this spell was cast from a graveyard, you may copy this spell and may choose a new target for
# the copy." A copy is not cast (CR 707.10), so it was cast from no zone: a copy of a flashed-back Reclamation does not offer
# a copy of itself (the card's ruling). On turn 3 Bot1 casts Reclamation from the hand for a spent Black Lotus, then flashes
# it back for the Lotus again and, with it on the stack, flashes in Lutri, the Spellchaser, whose trigger copies it with a
# new target, the Scalding Tarn cracked on turn 1. The copy returns the Tarn and asks nothing; the original, cast from the
# graveyard, returns the Lotus and offers its copy, which Bot1 takes (it has nothing left to return).

[Bot1 Deck]
Scalding Tarn
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Sevinne's Reclamation
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Scalding Tarn.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Scalding Tarn.Activate
Bot1.Search(Mountain)
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Sevinne's Reclamation.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Black Lotus)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Sevinne's Reclamation.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Black Lotus; Ability: Flashback)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lutri, the Spellchaser.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Scalding Tarn)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Exile = Sevinne's Reclamation
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mountain; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Lutri, the Spellchaser; Scalding Tarn; Black Lotus
